L8: 【2†Edit this Page†github.com】 【3†GitHub Project†github.com】 【4†Stack Overflow†stackoverflow.com】
L9: 
L10:  | For the latest stable version, please use 【5†Spring Boot 4.2.0】!
L11: # Calling REST Services
L12: 
L13: Spring Boot provides various convenient ways to call remote REST services. If you are developing a non-blocking reactive application and you’re using Spring WebFlux, then you can use 【6†`WebClient`】. If you prefer imperative APIs then you can use 【7†`RestClient`】 or 【8†`RestTemplate`】.
L14: ## WebClient
L15: 
L16: If you have Spring WebFlux on your classpath we recommend that you use 【6†`WebClient`】 to call remote REST services. The 【6†`WebClient`】 interface provides a functional style API and is fully reactive. You can learn more about the 【6†`WebClient`】 in the dedicated 【9†section in the Spring Framework docs】.
L17:  | If you are not writing a reactive Spring WebFlux application you can use the 【10†`RestClient`】 instead of a 【6†`WebClient`】. This provides a similar functional API, but is imperative rather than reactive.
L18: Spring Boot creates and pre-configures a prototype 【11†`WebClient.Builder`】 bean for you. It is strongly advised to inject it in your components and use it to create 【6†`WebClient`】 instances. Spring Boot is configuring that builder to share HTTP resources and reflect codecs setup in the same fashion as the server ones (see 【12†WebFlux HTTP codecs auto-configuration】), and more.
L19: 
L20: The following code shows a typical example:
L21: 
L22:   * Java
L23:   * Kotlin
L24: 
L25:     `import reactor.core.publisher.Mono;
L26: 
L27:     import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
L28:     import org.springframework.web.reactive.function.client.WebClient;
L29: 
L30:     @Service
L31:     public class MyService {
L32: 
L33:     	private final WebClient webClient;
L34: 
L35:     	public MyService(WebClient.Builder webClientBuilder) {
L36:     		this.webClient = webClientBuilder.baseUrl("https://example.org").build();
L37:     	}
L38: 
L39:     	public Mono<Details> someRestCall(String name) {
L40:     		return this.webClient.get().uri("/{name}/details", name).retrieve().bodyToMono(Details.class);
L41:     	}
L42: 
L43:     }`
L44: 
